    "field": "Land-atmosphere interaction",
    "problem": "Large variations exist among climate models regarding soil-moisture-precipitation feedbacks, and the mechanisms governing how mesoscale soil moisture patterns affect convective storm initiation in semi-arid regions are uncertain and poorly constrained by observations.",
    "method": "Using satellite observations of cloud cover and land surface temperature, we identify thousands of storm initiation points and statistically analyze the underlying surface conditions to demonstrate that convection is preferentially triggered over mesoscale soil-moisture gradients.",
    "task": "The task is to use satellite observations of land surface temperature and cloud cover over West Africa to determine how mesoscale variations in soil moisture affect the initiation of convective rain storms in the Sahel.",
